# release.sh gated Version.swift alone and four releases shipped a daemon whose
# /health said "0.1.0" (banshee-87l.15). The checker's whole value is the Cargo
# comparison; comparing the app version with itself makes it vacuously true and
# reproduces the shipped bug. The decoy-laden Cargo fixture in the test is what
# keeps a first-or-last `version =` read from passing too.
file: scripts/check-version-alignment.sh
test: test-version-alignment
---OLD---
if [ "$APP_VERSION" != "$CARGO_VERSION" ]; then
---NEW---
if [ "$APP_VERSION" != "$APP_VERSION" ]; then
